diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ba2013c..86baea4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -68,9 +68,12 @@ The legacy residual branch sees the complete flattened reference as well as the
 | `nearest` | Single nearest demonstration | No |
 | `nearest_residual` | Single nearest demonstration | Yes |
 | `cartesian` | Top-K Cartesian mixture | No |
+| `vinn_rbf` | Top-K RBF-weighted Cartesian mixture | No |
 | `cartesian_residual` | Top-K Cartesian mixture | Yes |
 | `latent_residual` | Decoded Top-K latent mixture | Yes |
 
+`vinn_rbf` is a VINN-style locally weighted regression baseline adapted to complete trajectories. It requires `retrieval_mode: rbf`, retrieves only from the training memory, averages the selected pose trajectories with normalized RBF weights, and has no residual network. The matched DeformPath configuration is `configs/deformpath_vinn_rbf.yaml`.
+
 Select methods with `--methods direct nearest_residual`, or edit the YAML list. The shared factories in `training/trainer.py` are the extension point for additional policy baselines.
 
 Retrieval residual policies accept `residual_mode: per_waypoint` (the backward-compatible default) or `residual_mode: constant`. The constant mode predicts one residual vector and broadcasts it across every waypoint:
@@ -85,7 +88,7 @@ For orientation-delta targets, this is one 12-value correction (six position and
 ### Training
 
 1. Fit per-channel trajectory mean/std from training trajectories only.
-2. Pretrain a common perception encoder using a temporary trajectory-regression head on training data. All six methods start from the same encoder parameters.
+2. Pretrain a common perception encoder using a temporary trajectory-regression head on training data. All configured methods start from the same encoder parameters.
 3. Train the trajectory autoencoder on training trajectories only, then freeze it for latent-reference prediction.
 4. Train each policy, selecting the checkpoint by validation trajectory MSE. The initial checkpoint is a candidate as well. Optional validation-loss early stopping checks the loss after every epoch, stops after the configured patience of non-improving epochs, and restores the best checkpoint.
 5. Evaluate on held-out episodes and export predictions and retrieval diagnostics.
diff --git a/configs/deformpath_vinn_rbf.yaml b/configs/deformpath_vinn_rbf.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bdc1c9f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/deformpath_vinn_rbf.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+seed: 7
+device: auto
+threads: 2
+horizon: 32
+
+data:
+  kind: deformpath
+  root: Deformapth2_camera1024_interpolated_nodbscan
+  source_root: DeformPath2_release/DeformPath/DeformPath2Bags
+  points: 1024
+  mode: segments
+  max_gap_seconds: 0.2
+  min_samples: 3
+  history_length: 8
+  history_window_seconds: 0.7
+  history_max_gap_seconds: 0.2
+  target_representation: xyz_quaternion
+
+pose_parameterization: orientation_delta
+
+encoder:
+  kind: pointnet
+  embedding_dim: 32
+  hidden_dim: 64
+
+history:
+  enabled: true
+  mode: full
+  hidden_dim: 64
+
+k: 100
+retrieval_mode: rbf
+retrieval_bandwidth: 0.15
+retrieval_all: false
+freeze_encoder: false
+pretrain_epochs: 20
+epochs: 1000
+batch_size: 32
+learning_rate: 0.001
+early_stopping:
+  enabled: true
+  patience: 30
+  min_delta: 0.0
+
+loss:
+  trajectory: 1.0
+  orientation: 1.0
+  residual: 0.0
+  acceleration: 0.0001
+  contrastive: 0.1
+
+methods: [vinn_rbf]
